// IOF Biopharma: the graph model and sample data
//
// Generated by ../../cypher.py from model.json and sample.json. Edit those and regenerate, rather than this file.
//
// Batch AB101-24-017 of a fictional monoclonal antibody, AB-101, made by a fictional biologics company, Aldermoor
// Biologics, at its Kilbride site. The data has the company as an enterprise, with a manufacturing operator; the
// site, its upstream area, the production process cell and its bioreactor unit, which holds a 2,000 L production
// bioreactor with its vessel, functions and capabilities, and a pH probe; the master recipe, and the batch's control
// recipe with its procedure, unit procedure, operation and feed phase; a working cell bank and the CHO cell line it
// holds; the production culture medium, classified by its supplier's catalog number, and its lot, whose certificate
// of analysis is granted after the supplier's quality control testing; the batch run, designated by its batch
// identifier, with its seed train, whose cell culture expansion proliferates the cells, the fed-batch production
// culture, the harvest and the Protein A capture step; the control strategy, with culture pH as a critical process
// parameter, set to 7.00 within a normal operating range of 6.90 to 7.10, and high molecular weight content as a
// critical quality attribute with a specification limit of 2.0 %; and the daily offline monitoring of viable cell
// density, which samples the culture and counts its cells.
//
// Run it against an empty database of Neo4j 5 or later, Enterprise Edition, for its node key and property existence
// constraints, e.g. with cypher-shell -f model.cypher. It merges every node and relationship, so it can be run again.

// The model: its constraints

